{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. Vitals before the doctor comes in. Sleeve up?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure one thirty-six over eighty-two. Pulse seventy-four. Temp thirty-six point nine Celsius. Oxygen sat ninety-seven percent.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (NURSE): List says lisinopril twenty milligrams every morning.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Um, no, that's wrong. The bottle says ten milligrams. Ten is what I give him.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (NURSE): Chart twenty, bottle ten. I'll flag both for the doctor.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He was on omeprazole. Well, actually he stopped it, back in March. Said it wasn't doing a thing.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (NURSE): Sucralfate, the Carafate they ordered?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Never picked it up. And the garage was packed, we drove in circles forever.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (NURSE): Rough. He's all yours.",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Stomach pain and not sleeping?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (DOCTOR): High up or low?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Middle.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (DOCTOR): Burning or crampy?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Burning.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Sorry, it's that burning pain. Every day for about three weeks, right under the breastbone. Comes after he eats and it wakes him.",
  "[SEG0021] person_4 (DOCTOR): Every day?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0023] person_4 (DOCTOR): Vomiting?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any black stool or blood?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (DOCTOR): And the sleep, every night?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Every night for a couple of months. He's up around two just lying there, even when the stomach's quiet.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Chest pain with it?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): Do you drink?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Socially.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (DOCTOR): Beer, wine, what?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Wine.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (CAREGIVER): It's a bottle of wine most nights, perhaps. I see the empties.",
  "[SEG0041] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fair?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Most nights.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (DOCTOR): Okay. No judgment from me. Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0045] person_4 (DOCTOR): Taking Advil?",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (CAREGIVER): A couple times a week. Two of those two-hundred milligram tablets.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0048] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0050] person_4 (DOCTOR): Abdomen's soft. Tender right at the top. No guarding.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (DOCTOR): Most likely gastritis from the wine and the Advil. An ulcer is still possible, I can't rule it out.",
  "[SEG0052] person_4 (DOCTOR): I'm ordering liver blood tests, a hepatic panel, given how much you're drinking. And we'll start omeprazole twenty milligrams every morning before breakfast.",
  "[SEG0053] person_4 (DOCTOR): Stop the Advil. Smaller meals, nothing after eight, ease up on the wine. Come back in two weeks for the labs."
 ],
